Design a voltage inverter circuit that outputs the logical inverse of input A when the enable signal TE is high. If TE is low, the output Z follows the state of A directly. The module utilizes p-type and n-type transistors to achieve the inversion, ensuring proper operation with the specified voltage supply rails.
module top_module(
    Z,
    A,
    TE
);

code:
module top_module(
    Z,
    A,
    TE
);output Z;
    input A;
    input TE;

    // Voltage supply signals
    supply1 VPWR;
    supply0 VGND;
    supply1 VPB;
    supply0 VNB;

    // Define n-type and p-type transistors as simple inverter gates
    wire n1_out;
    wire n1_in = A; // Connect A to n-type gate

    // n-type transistor (n1)
    assign n1_out = ~n1_in; // Logic for n-type transistor

    // p-type transistor (p1) based on output of n-type transistor
    assign Z = TE ? n1_out : A; // Inverter logic considering TE latch condition

endmodule

