Design a flip-flop circuit that operates on the negative edge of the clock (C). The circuit writes either a high value or the input data (D) to the output (SB_DFF_REG) based on the enable signal (E) and the set signal (S). If E is active and S is high, the output is set to 1. If E is active and S is low, the output takes the value of D. This module effectively acts as a dynamic register with configurable set/reset behavior.
