description:
Implement a circuit that swaps the middle two bytes of a 32-bit input. The output consists of the first byte unchanged, followed by the third byte, then the second byte, and finally the last byte, effectively rearranging the input bytes while preserving the outer bytes.
module top_module(
    input [31:0] in,
    output [31:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [31:0] in,
    output [31:0] out
);wire [7:0] byte1 = in[31:24];
    wire [7:0] byte2 = in[23:16];
    wire [7:0] byte3 = in[15:8];
    wire [7:0] byte4 = in[7:0];

    wire [15:0] temp = {byte3, byte2};

    assign out = {byte1, temp[15:8], temp[7:0], byte4};

endmodule

