description:
Create an n-bit wide ring counter that shifts its bits on each rising edge of the clock signal. The last bit of the counter is fed back to the first position, effectively creating a circular shift. The parameter 'n' defines the number of bits in the counter, allowing for flexibility in the size of the ring counter. The output presents the current state of the counter.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals

reg [n-1:0] counter;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  counter <= {counter[n-2:0], counter[n-1]};
end

assign out = counter;

endmodule

